# Maintainer git identity

The solo maintainer is the responsible party for every commit and PR in this
repo, even when an agent writes the diff.

## Commit author

Before any `git commit`, set author and committer to the maintainer. Do not
leave Cloud Agent defaults (`Cursor Agent` / `cursoragent@cursor.com`) on
commits that will be pushed.

```bash
export GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="markyjordan"
export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="37360049+markyjordan@users.noreply.github.com"
export GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="markyjordan"
export GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="37360049+markyjordan@users.noreply.github.com"
```

Repo-local `git config user.name` / `user.email` to the same values is fine for
a long session. Prefer the env exports when a managed global config would
otherwise win.

After committing, confirm with `git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>'`. If it is not
`markyjordan <37360049+markyjordan@users.noreply.github.com>`, amend only when
the commit is unpushed or the user explicitly allows rewrite.

## Topic branches

Use `marky/<type>/<slug>` for every PR head (examples: `marky/feat/...`,
`marky/fix/...`, `marky/chore/...`). Match `<type>` to the Conventional Commit
type of the change.

Do not open or push PR heads named `cursor/...`. If a Cloud Agent run template
defaults to `cursor/...`, create or retarget onto `marky/<type>/<slug>` instead
and use the PR tool's branch-prefix override when required.

Never push directly to `dev`, `main`, or `release/*`.
